---
/**
 * "How this site is secured". Every statement here must stay true; if a
 * control changes, update this page in the same change.
 * TODO(satish): rewrite in your own words so you can defend it in interviews.
 */
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="How this site is secured"
  description="How this portfolio is built and secured: a strict content security policy, no tracking, dependency controls and published contact details, grouped by NIST CSF 2.0."
  todo={['Rewrite this page in your own words (plan section 3.6).', 'Add the Mozilla HTTP Observatory grade and scan date after deploying.']}
>
  <div class="container page page--narrow">
    <h1 class="page__title">How this site is secured</h1>
    <p class="page__intro">
      This is a small static site, so the risks are small too: someone tampering with the content, a compromised dependency, or personal data
      being exposed. These are the controls in place, grouped by the six functions of the NIST Cybersecurity Framework 2.0.
    </p>

    <dl class="controls">
      <div class="controls__row">
        <dt>Govern</dt>
        <dd>
          Decisions are written down in the project's docs folder. New package versions are installed only after they have been public for 7
          days, and packages cannot run install scripts unless reviewed. Exceptions are pinned to one version and explained.
        </dd>
      </div>
      <div class="controls__row">
        <dt>Identify</dt>
        <dd>
          The assets are the site content, the contact channel and the accounts that publish the site. The site stores no visitor data and
          handles no logins.
        </dd>
      </div>
      <div class="controls__row">
        <dt>Protect</dt>
        <dd>
          A strict Content Security Policy allows scripts and styles only from this site (<code>script-src 'self'</code>, no inline code), and
          Trusted Types blocks unsafe DOM writes. Other headers enforce HTTPS, stop the site being framed, and turn off unused browser features.
          No cookies, analytics or third-party scripts. No phone number or street address is published.
        </dd>
      </div>
      <div class="controls__row">
        <dt>Detect</dt>
        <dd>
          Every build is checked automatically for inline code, placeholder text and oversized files, and fails if it finds any. Dependencies are
          audited for known vulnerabilities before release.
        </dd>
      </div>
      <div class="controls__row">
        <dt>Respond</dt>
        <dd>
          Security contact details are published in <a href="/.well-known/security.txt">security.txt</a> (RFC 9116).
        </dd>
      </div>
      <div class="controls__row">
        <dt>Recover</dt>
        <dd>The site is rebuilt from source control in minutes and holds no data that could be lost.</dd>
      </div>
    </dl>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
